H7900.definition:
from H5526 (סָכַךְ) in the sense of H7753 (שׂוּךְ);
a booth (as interlaced)
KJV: tabernacle.

H7901.definition:
a primitive root;
to lie down (for rest, sexual connection, decease or any other purpose)
KJV: [idiom] at all, cast down, (lover-)lay (self) (down), (make to) lie (down, down to sleep, still with), lodge, ravish, take rest, sleep, stay.

H7902.definition:
from H7901 (שָׁכַב);
a lying down (of dew, or for the sexual act)
KJV: [idiom] carnally, copulation, [idiom] lay, seed.

H7903.definition:
from H7901 (שָׁכַב);
a (sexual) lying with
KJV: [idiom] lie.

H7904.definition:
a primitive root;
to roam (through lust)
KJV: in the morning (by mistake for H7925 (שָׁכַם)).

H7905.definition:
feminine of H7900 (שֹׂךְ) in the sense of H7899 (שֵׂךְ);
a dart (as pointed like a thorn)
KJV: barbed iron.

H7906.definition:
from an unused root apparently meaning to surmount; an observatory (with the article);
Seku, a place in Palestine
KJV: Sechu.

H7907.definition:
from the same as H7906 (שֵׂכוּ);
observant, i.e. (concretely) the mind
KJV: heart.

H7908.definition:
infinitive of H7921 (שָׁכֹל);
bereavement
KJV: loss of children, spoiling.

H7909.definition:
or שַׁכֻּל; from H7921 (שָׁכֹל);
bereaved
KJV: barren, bereaved (robbed) of children (whelps).

H7910.definition:
or שִׁכֹּר; from H7937 (שָׁכַר);
intoxicated, as astate or a habit
KJV: drunk(-ard, -en, -en man).

H7911.definition:
or שָׁכֵחַ; a primitive root;
to mislay, i.e. to be oblivious of, from want of memory or attention
KJV: [idiom] at all, (cause to) forget.

H7912.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H7911 (שָׁכַח) through the idea of disclosure of a covered or forgotten thing;
to discover (literally or figuratively)
KJV: find.

H7914.definition:
feminine from the same as H7906 (שֵׂכוּ);
a conspicuous object
KJV: picture.

H7915.definition:
intensive perhaps from the same as H7906 (שֵׂכוּ) in the sense of H7753 (שׂוּךְ);
a knife (as pointed or edged)
KJV: knife.

H7916.definition:
from H7936 (שָׂכַר);
a man at wages  by the day or year
KJV: hired (man, servant), hireling.

H7917.definition:
feminine of H7916 (שָׂכִיר);
a hiring
KJV: that is hired.

H7918.definition:
a primitive root;
to weave (i.e. lay) a trap; figuratively, (through the idea of secreting) to allay (passions; physically, abate a flood)
KJV: appease, assuage, make to cease, pacify, set.

H7919.definition:
a primitive root;
to be (causatively, make or act) circumspect and hence, intelligent
KJV: consider, expert, instruct, prosper, (deal) prudent(-ly), (give) skill(-ful), have good success, teach, (have, make to) understand(-ing), wisdom, (be, behave self, consider, make) wise(-ly), guide wittingly.

H7920.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H7919 (שָׂכַל)
{to be (causatively, make or act) circumspect and hence, intelligent}
KJV: consider.

H7921.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to miscarry, i.e. suffer abortion; by analogy, to bereave (literally or figuratively)
KJV: bereave (of children), barren, cast calf (fruit, young), be (make) childless, deprive, destroy, [idiom] expect, lose children, miscarry, rob of children, spoil.

H7922.definition:
or שֵׂכֶל; from H7919 (שָׂכַל);
intelligence; by implication, success
KJV: discretion, knowledge, policy, prudence, sense, understanding, wisdom, wise.

H7923.definition:
plural from H7921 (שָׁכֹל);
childlessness (by continued bereavements)
KJV: to have after loss of others.

H7925.definition:
a primitive root; properly, to incline (the shoulder to a burden); but used only as denominative from H7926 (שְׁכֶם);
literally, to load up (on the back of man or beast), i.e. to start early in the morning
KJV: (arise, be up, get (oneself) up, rise up) early (betimes), morning.

H7926.definition:
from H7925 (שָׁכַם);
the neck (between the shoulders) as the place of burdens; figuratively, the spur of ahill
KJV: back, [idiom] consent, portion, shoulder.

H7927.definition:
the same as H7926 (שְׁכֶם); ridge;
Shekem, a place in Palestine
KJV: Shechem.

H7928.definition:
for H7926 (שְׁכֶם);
Shekem, the name of a Hivite and two Israelites
KJV: Shechem.

H7929.definition:
feminine of H7926 (שְׁכֶם);
the shoulderbone
KJV: shoulder blade.

H7930.definition:
patronymic from H7928 (שֶׁכֶם);
a Shikmite (collectively), or descendants of Shekem
KJV: Shichemites.

H7931.definition:
a primitive root (apparently akin (by transmission) to H7901 (שָׁכַב) through the idea of lodging; compare H5531 (סִכְלוּת), H7925 (שָׁכַם));
to reside or permanently stay (literally or figuratively)
KJV: abide, continue, (cause to, make to) dwell(-er), have habitation, inhabit, lay, place, (cause to) remain, rest, set (up).

H7932.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H7931 (שָׁכַן)
{to reside or permanently stay (literally or figuratively)}
KJV: cause to dwell, have habitation.

H7933.definition:
from H7931 (שָׁכַן);
a residence
KJV: habitation.

H7934.definition:
from H7931 (שָׁכַן);
a resident; by extension, a fellow-citizen
KJV: inhabitant, neighbour, nigh.

H7935.definition:
or (prolonged) שְׁכַנְיָהוּ; from H7931 (שָׁכַן) and H3050 (יָהּ); Jah has dwelt;
Shekanjah, the name of nine Israelites
KJV: Shecaniah, Shechaniah.

H7936.definition:
or (by permutation) סָכַר; (Ezra 4:5), a primitive root (apparently akin (by prosthesis) to H3739 (כָּרָה) through the idea of temporary purchase; compare H7937 (שָׁכַר));
to hire
KJV: earn wages, hire (out self), reward, [idiom] surely.

H7937.definition:
a primitive root;
to become tipsy; in a qualified sense, to satiate with astimulating drink or (figuratively) influence
KJV: (be filled with) drink (abundantly), (be, make) drunk(-en), be merry. (Superlative of H8248 (שָׁקָה).)

H7938.definition:
from H7936 (שָׂכַר);
wages
KJV: reward, sluices.

H7939.definition:
from H7936 (שָׂכַר);
payment of contract; concretely, salary, fare, maintenance; by implication, compensation, benefit
KJV: hire, price, reward(-ed), wages, worth.

H7940.definition:
the same as H7939 (שָׂכָר); recompense;
Sakar, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Sacar.

H7941.definition:
from H7937 (שָׁכַר);
an intoxicant, i.e. intensely alcoholic liquor
KJV: strong drink, [phrase] drunkard, strong wine.

H7942.definition:
for H7943 (שִׁכָּרוֹן);
drunkenness, Shikkeron, a place in Palestine
KJV: Shicron.

H7944.definition:
from H7952 (שָׁלָה) abbreviated form;
a fault
KJV: error.

H7945.definition:
for the rel. H834 (אֲשֶׁר); used with prepositional prefix, and often followed by some pronominal affix;
on account of, whatsoever, whichsoever
KJV: cause, sake.

H7946.definition:
for H7600 (שַׁאֲנָן);
tranquil
KJV: being at ease.

H7947.definition:
a primitive root;
to space off; intensive (evenly) to make equidistant
KJV: equally distant, set in order.

H7948.definition:
from H7947 (שָׁלַב);
a spacer or raised interval, i.e. the stile in aframe or panel
KJV: ledge.

H7949.definition:
a primitive root; properly, meaning to be white; used only as denominative from H7950 (שֶׁלֶג);
to be snow-white (with the linen clothing of the slain)
KJV: be as snow.

H7950.definition:
from H7949 (שָׁלַג);
snow (probably from its whiteness)
KJV: snow(-y).

H7951.definition:
or שָׁלַו; (Job 3:26), a primitive root;
to be tranquil, i.e. secure or successful
KJV: be happy, prosper, be in safety.

H7952.definition:
a primitive root (probably identical with H7953 (שָׁלָה) through the idea of educing);
to mislead
KJV: deceive, be negligent.

H7953.definition:
a primitive root (rather cognate (by contraction) to the base of H5394 (נָשַׁל), H7997 (שָׁלַל) and their congeners through the idea of extracting);
to draw out or off, i.e. remove (the soul by death)
KJV: take away.

H7954.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H7951 (שָׁלָה);
to be secure
KJV: at rest.

H7955.definition:
(Aramaic) from a root corresponding to H7952 (שָׁלָה);
a wrong
KJV: thing amiss.

H7956.definition:
the same as H7596 (שְׁאֵלָה) (shortened); request;
Shelah, the name of a postdiluvian patriarch and of an Israelite
KJV: Shelah.

H7957.definition:
from the same as H3851 (לַהַב) with sibilant prefix;
a flare of fire
KJV: (flaming) flame.

H7958.definition:
or שְׂלָיו; by orthographical variation from H7951 (שָׁלָה) through the idea of sluggishness;
the quail collectively (as slow in flight from its weight)
KJV: quails.

H7960.definition:
(Aramaic) or שָׁלוּת; (Aramaic), from the same as H7955 (שָׁלָה);
a fault
KJV: error, [idiom] fail, thing amiss.

H7961.definition:
or שָׁלֵיו; feminine שְׁלֵוָה; from H7951 (שָׁלָה);
tranquil; (in a bad sense) careless; abstractly, security
KJV: (being) at ease, peaceable, (in) prosper(-ity), quiet(-ness), wealthy.

H7962.definition:
from H7951 (שָׁלָה);
security (genuine or false)
KJV: abundance, peace(-ably), prosperity, quietness.

H7963.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H7962 (שַׁלְוָה);
safety
KJV: tranquillity. See also H7961 (שָׁלֵו).

H7964.definition:
or שִׁלֻּחַ; from H7971 (שָׁלַח);
(only in plural) a dismissal, i.e. (of a wife) divorce (especially the document); also (of a daughter) dower
KJV: presents, have sent back.

H7965.definition:
or שָׁלֹם; from H7999 (שָׁלַם);
safe, i.e. (figuratively) well, happy, friendly; also (abstractly) welfare, i.e. health, prosperity, peace
KJV: [idiom] do, familiar, [idiom] fare, favour, [phrase] friend, [idiom] great, (good) health, ([idiom] perfect, such as be at) peace(-able, -ably), prosper(-ity, -ous), rest, safe(-ty), salute, welfare, ([idiom] all is, be) well, [idiom] wholly.

H7966.definition:
or שִׁלֻּם; from H7999 (שָׁלַם);
a requital, i.e. (secure) retribution, (venal) a fee
KJV: recompense, reward.

H7967.definition:
or (shorter) שַׁלֻּם; the same as H7966 (שִׁלּוּם);
Shallum, the name of fourteen Israelites
KJV: Shallum.

H7968.definition:
probably for H7967 (שַׁלּוּם);
Shallun, an Israelite
KJV: Shallum.

H7969.definition:
or שָׁלֹשׁ; masculine שְׁלוֹשָׁה; or שְׁלֹשָׁה; a primitive number;
three; occasionally (ordinal) third, or (multiple) thrice
KJV: [phrase] fork, [phrase] often(-times), third, thir(-teen, -teenth), three, [phrase] thrice. Compare H7991 (שָׁלִישׁ).

H7970.definition:
or שְׁלֹשִׁים; multiple of H7969 (שָׁלוֹשׁ);
thirty; or (ordinal) thirtieth
KJV: thirty, thirtieth. Compare H7991 (שָׁלִישׁ).

H7971.definition:
a primitive root;
to send away, for, or out (in a great variety of applications)
KJV: [idiom] any wise, appoint, bring (on the way), cast (away, out), conduct, [idiom] earnestly, forsake, give (up), grow long, lay, leave, let depart (down, go, loose), push away, put (away, forth, in, out), reach forth, send (away, forth, out), set, shoot (forth, out), sow, spread, stretch forth (out).

H7972.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H7971 (שָׁלַח)
{to send away, for, or out (in a great variety of applications)}
KJV: put, send.

H7973.definition:
from H7971 (שָׁלַח);
a missile of attack, i.e. spear; also (figuratively) a shoot of growth; i.e. branch
KJV: dart, plant, [idiom] put off, sword, weapon.

H7974.definition:
the same as H7973 (שֶׁלַח);
Shelach, a postdiluvian patriarch
KJV: Salah, Shelah. Compare H7975 (שִׁלֹחַ)lemma שִׁלֹּחַ extra dagesh, corrected to שִׁלֹחַ.

H7975.definition:
or (in imitation of H7974 (שֶׁלַח)) שֶׁלַח; (Nehemiah 3:15), from H7971 (שָׁלַח); rill;
Shiloach, a fountain of Jerusalem
KJV: Shiloah, Siloah.

H7976.definition:
feminine of H7964 (שִׁלּוּחַ);
a shoot
KJV: branch.

H7977.definition:
from H7973 (שֶׁלַח); missive, i.e. armed;
Shilchi, an Israelite
KJV: Shilhi.

H7978.definition:
plural of H7973 (שֶׁלַח); javelins or sprouts;
Shilchim, a place in Palestine
KJV: Shilhim.

H7979.definition:
from H7971 (שָׁלַח);
a table (as spread out); by implication, a meal
KJV: table.

H7980.definition:
a primitive root;
to dominate, i.e. govern; by implication, to permit
KJV: (bear, have) rule, have dominion, give (have) power.

H7981.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H7980 (שָׁלַט)
{to dominate, i.e. govern; by implication, to permit}
KJV: have the mastery, have power, bear rule, be (make) ruler.

H7982.definition:
from H7980 (שָׁלַט);
probably a shield (as controlling, i.e. protecting the person)
KJV: shield.

H7984.definition:
(Aramaic) or שִׁלְטֹןlemma שִׁלְטן missing vowel, corrected to שִׁלְטֹן; corresponding to H7983 (שִׁלְטוֹן)
{a potentate}
KJV: ruler.

H7985.definition:
(Aramaic) from H7981 (שְׁלֵט);
empire (abstractly or concretely)
KJV: dominion.

H7986.definition:
feminine from H7980 (שָׁלַט);
a vixen
KJV: imperious.

H7988.definition:
feminine from H7953 (שָׁלָה);
a fetus or babe (as extruded in birth)
KJV: young one.

H7989.definition:
from H7980 (שָׁלַט);
potent; concretely, a prince or warrior
KJV: governor, mighty, that hath power, ruler.

H7990.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H7989 (שַׁלִּיט);
mighty; abstractly, permission; concretely, a premier
KJV: captain, be lawful, rule(-r).

H7991.definition:
or שָׁלוֹשׁ; (1 Chronicles 11:11; 1 Chronicles 12:18), or שָׁלֹשׁ; (2 Samuel 23:13), from H7969 (שָׁלוֹשׁ);
a triple, i.e. (as a musical instrument) a triangle (or perhaps rather threestringed lute); also (as an indefinite, great quantity) a three-fold measure (perhaps a treble ephah); also (as an officer) a general of the third rank (upward, i.e. the highest)
KJV: captain, instrument of musick, (great) lord, (great) measure, prince, three (from the margin).

H7992.definition:
ordinal from H7969 (שָׁלוֹשׁ);
third; feminine athird (part); by extension, a third (day, year or time); specifically, a third-story cell)
KJV: third (part, rank, time), three (years old).

H7993.definition:
a primitive root;
to throw out, down or away (literally or figuratively)
KJV: adventure, cast (away, down, forth, off, out), hurl, pluck, throw.

H7994.definition:
from H7993 (שָׁלַךְ);
bird of prey, usually thought to be the pelican (from casting itself into the sea)
KJV: cormorant.

H7995.definition:
from H7993 (שָׁלַךְ);
a felling (of trees)
KJV: when cast.

H7996.definition:
the same as H7995 (שַׁלֶּכֶת);
Shalleketh, a gate in Jerusalem
KJV: Shalleketh.

H7997.definition:
a primitive root;
to drop or strip; by implication, to plunder
KJV: let fall, make self a prey, [idiom] of purpose, (make a, (take)) spoil.

H7998.definition:
from H7997 (שָׁלַל);
booty
KJV: prey, spoil.

H7999.definition:
a primitive root;
to be safe (in mind, body or estate); figuratively, to be (causatively, make) completed; by implication, to be friendly; by extension, to reciprocate (in various applications)
KJV: make amends, (make an) end, finish, full, give again, make good, (re-) pay (again), (make) (to) (be at) peace(-able), that is perfect, perform, (make) prosper(-ous), recompense, render, requite, make restitution, restore, reward, [idiom] surely.
